{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-019", "content_sha256": "0dea73f5654ce880bc727337c3942b76e65f7d4bd7640c804b9dbe1e00add444", "heading": "MS-019", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-018", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "251b46ba0bd9a08d66d57eca44fc8c80cd283289"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-019", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": false, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-019", "text": "### MS-019 — ALLOW: permitted variants of the required answer\n\n**Claim:** ALLOW grants variants of the same underlying answer, including partial\ndescriptions.\n**Evidence:** \"ALLOW black / ALLOW any combination of grey and black eg grey-black\"\non the colour-completion task (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 60-74).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-020", "content_sha256": "8eb2cabb280941f7e99ae776765e4eb2e643f991a71c0daed0410c3c3a1d8166", "heading": "MS-020", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-018", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "251b46ba0bd9a08d66d57eca44fc8c80cd283289"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-020", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": false, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-020", "text": "### MS-020 — ACCEPT: equivalent responses to method points\n\n**Claim:** ACCEPT admits an equivalent formulation of a method or action point.\n**Evidence:** \"M1 add chlorine (solution) to potassium bromide ACCEPT mix the two\n(solutions) solutions\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 96-110).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-021", "content_sha256": "6ab31d956546753d318304d2314084867aa44d651881bb71281ca8a9ba1c8c34", "heading": "MS-021", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-018", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "251b46ba0bd9a08d66d57eca44fc8c80cd283289"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-021", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": false, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-021", "text": "### MS-021 — Observation and product-form alternatives\n\n**Claim:** observation and product statements accept alternative phrasings printed\ninline.\n**Evidence:** \"M2 (solution) turns orange ALLOW any combination of\norange/yellow/brown\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 96-110);\nthe parsed excerpt\n(SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 98-112).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-022", "content_sha256": "502797ec8e06aea8e500810b4f92d449e7bb6c807f7b66d1b1f5fd966b32474c", "heading": "MS-022", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-018", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "251b46ba0bd9a08d66d57eca44fc8c80cd283289"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-022", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": false, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-022", "text": "### MS-022 — Reverse-argument acceptance\n\n**Claim:** some conclusion points explicitly accept the inverse reasoning route.\n**Evidence:** \"M4 (therefore) chlorine is more reactive (than bromine) ACCEPT\nreverse argument\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 110-124).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-023", "content_sha256": "95aaae09ef62b08598f5d32b3033005c6b8ab34af1e2703031dd61307e077d9e", "heading": "MS-023", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-018", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "251b46ba0bd9a08d66d57eca44fc8c80cd283289"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-023", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": false, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-023", "text": "### MS-023 — Name/symbol pairs as printed alternatives\n\n**Claim:** chemical names and formulae are printed as interchangeable pairs in both\nanswers and allowances.\n**Evidence:** \"bromine/Br2\" across the displacement scheme's points (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 116-130); the noble-gas pair \"argon and helium\nALLOW Ar and He\" on the 2CR atmosphere item .\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-024", "content_sha256": "b4012e2fba6c47038a32c60634e3a662ff085fa8268a245140b3f4680e50cf84", "heading": "MS-024", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-018", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "251b46ba0bd9a08d66d57eca44fc8c80cd283289"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-024", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": false, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-024", "text": "### MS-024 — Alternative scoring routes\n\n**Claim:** a point can name a second route by which it may be earned.\n**Evidence:** \"M3 can be scored by Br2 as a product in an equation\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 110-124).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-058", "content_sha256": "538bd5a6e75e0bb4ff4618dd43aeef0db305ab636d7921fd40e64c69e4001d5e", "heading": "MS-058", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-018", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "251b46ba0bd9a08d66d57eca44fc8c80cd283289"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-058", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": false, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-058", "text": "### MS-058 — Synonym-level allowances at the vocabulary layer\n\n**Claim:** the alternative machinery operates below the phrase level: single words are granted as substitutes (combination for mixture) while a neighbouring cell fences off the chemically wrong vocabulary (compound, or any bonding reference). The allowance and the rejection are adjacent cells of the same point, so the alternative space is defined jointly — what may be swapped, and what may never be. Vocabulary-level tolerance is thus printed, bounded, and as authoritative as the answer itself.\n**Evidence:** the alloy-definition point grants \"ALLOW combination for mixture\" and, in the adjoining cell, \"REJECT compound or references to chemical bonding\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 265-279).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-059", "content_sha256": "7a11f15b8fd7d3d3f2d796276e58ea07e9ce5e936042d5fe33dd3616e153ae45", "heading": "MS-059", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-018", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "251b46ba0bd9a08d66d57eca44fc8c80cd283289"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-059", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": false, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-059", "text": "### MS-059 — Reference-scoped allowances: any named instance from a printed set\n\n**Claim:** allowances can be scoped to a reference set rather than enumerated inline: the safety point admits any named alcohol from the question's own table, converting the table into part of the acceptance space. The same point's allowance cell paraphrases the ignition wording (can be easily ignited) while the answer line fixes the chemical fact (flammable). The scope form keeps the scheme compact where the candidate's choice of instance is chemically irrelevant.\n**Evidence:** the Bunsen-safety point answers \"alcohols/the liquids are flammable/catch fire\" with the paraphrase allowance and the scoped extension \"ALLOW any named alcohol from the table\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 145-159).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "MS-04", "chunk_id": "MS-04:rec:MS-060", "content_sha256": "455a16e4e3d28c4ca20314365b235c1a52ef3af90059e64df3893ac135462bb0", "heading": "MS-060", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "MS-04", "artifact_version": 1.1, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-018", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "2cb92fe5f56d22f1b231c129a7e0dbc27bf86007", "syllabai_resources": "251b46ba0bd9a08d66d57eca44fc8c80cd283289"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "MS-060", "research_family": "mark_scheme_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": false, "supplementary": false, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "MS-060", "text": "### MS-060 — Numeric-value allowances on calculated results\n\n**Claim:** alternatives extend to the numbers themselves: a calculation point can print the variants of the accepted value — a rounding neighbour admitted outright — and a band of values earned from a different data route, each priced at its own mark. The mean-time item grants 62.3 beside 62, and the misread-data band 69, 69.25 and 69.3 for one mark. Numeric acceptance is therefore a printed boundary, not marker generosity, and it is priced per route.\n**Evidence:** the mean calculation grants \"ALLOW 62.3\" beside the exact mean and states \"62/62.3 with no working scores 2\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 159-173); the misread-data band prints \"ALLOW 69/69.25/69.3 for 1 mark\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 172-186).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
